      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: don't mark exact-size responses as truncated in readResponseText",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n**Problem**: `readResponseText` unconditionally marked a response as truncated when `bytesRead >= maxBytes`, even when the body was exactly the limit with no bytes omitted. `web_fetch` then surfaced a misleading \"Response body truncated\" warning to users.\n\n**Solution**: When `bytesRead` reaches `maxBytes` without prior truncation, peek one more `reader.read()` call to confirm whether EOF was reached. Only mark truncated if the next read returns data (`!done || value.byteLength > 0`). An exact-size body returns `truncated: false`.\n\n**What changed**: `web-shared.ts`: Split the `truncated || bytesRead >= maxBytes` condition into two branches — immediate break for known-truncated, peek+confirm before declaring truncation for exact-limit. `web-shared.test.ts`: Added `\"treats exact-limit responses as complete, not truncated\"` test.\n\n**What did NOT change**: The `readResponseText` API contract. Web-fetch truncation warning logic. Under-limit and genuine-overflow behavior.\n\nFixes #101837\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`web_fetch` could report a false \"Response body truncated after N bytes\" warning when the response body was exactly N bytes. The truncation check at `web-shared.ts:275` treated `bytesRead >= maxBytes` the same as genuine overflow, without confirming whether more data existed.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`readResponseText` line 275-276:\n```typescript\nif (truncated || bytesRead >= maxBytes) {\n  truncated = true;  // Bug: fires even when body is exactly maxBytes\n  break;\n}\n```\n\nWhen chunks add up to exactly `maxBytes` with no overflow, `truncated` was still set to `true`.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n**Behavior addressed**: Exact-size response bodies return `truncated: false` with no reader cancellation\n\n**Real environment tested**: Linux x86_64, Node 24.13.1\n\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**:\n```terminal\npnpm test -- src/agents/tools/web-shared.test.ts src/agents/tools/web-fetch.test.ts\n```\n\n**After-fix evidence**:\n```terminal_output\n✓ treats exact-limit responses as complete, not truncated\n✓ cancels and releases bounded response readers after truncation\n✓ releases bounded response readers after complete reads\n\nweb-shared.test.ts  12 passed (12)\nweb-fetch.test.ts   14 passed (14)\nTOTAL               26 passed (26)\n```\n\nThe new test uses a 5-byte \"hello\" chunk with maxBytes=5, verifies `truncated: false`, `bytesRead: 5`, and `cancel` not called.\n\n**Observed result after the fix**: Exact-limit bodies return `truncated: false`. Genuine overflow still returns `truncated: true` (existing tests pass). Under-limit complete reads unchanged.\n\n**What was not tested**: End-to-end web_fetch with a real HTTP server returning exactly maxResponseBytes. The unit test covers the exact same code path.\n\n## Risk checklist\n\nmerge-risk: Low\n\n- [x] Low risk — one additional `reader.read()` at the exact limit only\n- [x] All 26 existing + new tests pass\n- [x] 2 files changed, +30/-2 = net +28 lines\n- [x] Under-limit and genuine-overflow behavior unchanged\n- [x] No breaking API changes",
        "branch": "fix/issue-101837-webfetch-exact-size-trunc",
